scenario: batch_out_of_time_order
Events are emitted when a request ends, so a batch is not in time order. The place is first seen at its earliest event, which is where the detection takes its time and its evidence from: here the earlier request, from 203.0.113.9, though the later one is listed first.

step 1  0h       app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 openai-python/3
  nothing raised

step 2  24h      app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 openai-python/3
  nothing raised

step 3  48h      app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 openai-python/3
  nothing raised

step 4  72h      app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 openai-python/3
  nothing raised

step 5  8d       one batch of 2 events
        8d10m    app     request  198.51.100.9 DE AS64500 openai-python/3
        8d       app     request  203.0.113.9 DE AS64500 openai-python/3
  detection #1 incident 1: new_country high
      observed new country DE
      baseline US (4 requests)
      from     203.0.113.9
      network  203.0.113.0/24
      country  DE
      as       AS64500 Example Net
      client   openai-python/3
  detection #2 incident 1: new_network low
      observed new network
      baseline 1 usual network
      usual    198.51.100.0/24 (5 requests)
      from     203.0.113.9
      network  203.0.113.0/24
      country  DE
      as       AS64500 Example Net
      client   openai-python/3
  alert: incident 1 opened, high, rules [new_country new_network], about new_country

incidents at the end:
  #1 app open high rules [new_country new_network], 2 detections, opened 192h0m0s, last fired 192h0m0s
